.TH "SVGANIMATEDENUMERATION.BASEVAL" "3JS" "June 26, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGAnimatedEnumeration.baseVal \- SVGAnimatedEnumeration: baseVal
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]baseVal\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] interface represents the value of an
SVG enumeration.
.SH VALUE
An integer representing the base value of the enumeration.
Ths is the non\-animated content value of the corresponding attribute.
.PP
The allowed values depend on the attribute that is reflected.
.SH EXCEPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if the property is set to a constant that is not in the set of
defined enumerations, or to \f[CR]0\f[R], which represents the
\(lqunknown attribute\(rq value.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
Consider this snippet with a \f[CR]<clipPath>\f[R] element: Its
\f[CR]clipPathUnits\f[R] is associated with an
\f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] object.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R] viewBox=\(dq0 0 100 100\(dq width=\(dq200\(dq height=\(dq200\(dq>
  <\f[B]clipPath\f[R] id=\(dqclip1\(dq clipPathUnits=\(dquserSpaceOnUse\(dq>
    <\f[B]circle\f[R] cx=\(dq50\(dq cy=\(dq50\(dq r=\(dq35\(dq />
  </\f[B]clipPath\f[R]>

  \f[I]<!\-\- Some reference rect to materialized to clip path \-\->\f[R]
  <\f[B]rect\f[R] id=\(dqr1\(dq x=\(dq0\(dq y=\(dq0\(dq width=\(dq45\(dq height=\(dq45\(dq />
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
The following JavaScript gets the element, and logs the
\f[CR]baseVal\f[R] of the \f[CR]SVGClipPathElement.clipPathUnits\f[R]
property.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] clipPathElt = document.getElementById(\(dqclip1\(dq);
console.log(clipPathElt.clipPathUnits.baseVal); \f[I]// Logs 1 that correspond to userSpaceOnUse\f[R]
.EE
